<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="S-2238.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>S-2238.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>SENATE BILL 6141</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>60th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2007 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Senators Jacobsen and Morton</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 02/28/2007.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Natural Resources, Ocean &amp; Recreation.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Expanding provisions affecting forest health.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to forest health; and creating a new section.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="new"><LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>The legislature finds that Washington<LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4"/>currently faces forest health threats.  In response to these threats,<LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5"/>the legislature intends to create a comprehensive forest health program<LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6"/>for the state.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 1	SB 6141</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>